<theme xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:framework:Config/etc/theme.xsd">
    <title>Spartrak RTL</title>
    <!--
      PARENT CHANGED 2026-08-24: was Smartwave/porto_rtl, now Spartrak/spartrak.

      WHY: with porto_rtl as the parent, this theme was a SIBLING of
      Spartrak/spartrak rather than a descendant, so Magento's theme fallback
      never let it see any Spartrak-authored template, layout, JS or LESS.
      Every shared file had to be physically duplicated into both theme trees
      — which had already silently drifted and produced three real bugs (the
      RTL theme was missing the PLP filter-toggle RequireJS mapping, the
      "Shop by categories" nav CTA, and the Top Promo Banner + utility strip
      layout additions).

      Making this theme a real child of Spartrak/spartrak gives exactly the
      single-source-of-truth model Porto itself uses (porto_rtl -> porto):
      write shared implementation once in Spartrak/spartrak, and keep only
      genuinely direction-specific overrides here.

      Chain is now: Spartrak/spartrak_rtl -> Spartrak/spartrak
                    -> Smartwave/porto -> Magento/blank

      Smartwave/porto_rtl is no longer in the chain. Everything it actually
      contributed was audited and absorbed into this theme, because all of it
      is genuinely RTL-specific and belongs in an RTL theme anyway:
        - Smartwave_Porto/templates/html/head.phtml (loads bootstrap.rtl.css /
          the .rtl header CSS variants and sets js_porto_vars.rtl = "1")
        - <body class="rtl"> (see this theme's Magento_Theme/layout/default.xml)
        - its 15 RTL LESS source overrides + animate.css under web/css/
          (Magento/blank's styles-m.less @imports source/_theme.less,
          source/_variables.less etc. by relative path, so this theme's copies
          now win by fallback exactly as porto_rtl's did before)
      porto_rtl's own etc/view.xml is intentionally NOT absorbed: it was the
      source of the RTL PDP gallery crash (it redeclared the whole `gallery`
      var block while omitting `thumbmargin`), and dropping it out of the chain
      fixes that bug at the root.

      See .claude/docs/10-THEME-ARCHITECTURE.md for the full decision record
      and the rule for what belongs here vs. in Spartrak/spartrak vs. in a
      shared module.
    -->
    <parent>Spartrak/spartrak</parent>
</theme>
